-- title:
--   The filtering host computes its parameters and sets up its frame
-- statement:
--   In a program $P$ that holds the procedures for $\log_2$, integer square root, powers of two and division (`ParamProcs`), for an all-edges instance $x$ with $n,U\ge1$, a free pointer $f$ and limits whose space, word size and depth allow the host (`aTOP x.n fr ≤ lim.space`, `filterWord n U ≤ lim.word`, $d<$ depth), the statement `paramsStmt`, run in the frame $[n,U,ab,bc,ac,out,f]$, ends within `tParams n U` steps with the memory unchanged and the frame `topFrame x fr` holding the parameters of the filtering host.
